  "prompt": "What were the step rates of the 2024 sales funnel? Take the leads created in 2024 (created_at, Brussels local time). A contact is one email address, compared exactly as stored. A contact counts as with_opportunity when one of those leads has an opportunity, and as won when one of those opportunities is won. The steps need no date order: an opportunity counts whenever it was created, and a won one whenever it closed, even in a later year. Return five columns, in this order: contacts, with_opportunity, won (each a number of contacts), opportunity_rate (with_opportunity over contacts) and win_rate (won over with_opportunity), each rate a fraction between 0 and 1. Return one row. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "contacts",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "with_opportunity",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "won",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "opportunity_rate",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
